bcSection\" data-content=\"offense\"><h4>Offense</h4><hr /><strong>Speed</strong><ul class=\"sbcCommaList\" data-content=\"speed\">  <li>Land 40 ft</li>  </ul><br />  <strong>Melee</strong> bite +2 (1d4+1)<br />   <ul class=\"sbcSemicolonList\">   </ul>   </div></div>    <div class=\"sbcSection\" data-content=\"statistics\"><h4>Statistics</h4><hr /><ul class=\"sbcCommaList\" data-content=\"attributes\"><li><strong>Str</strong> 13</li><li><strong>Dex</strong> 13</li><li><strong>Con</strong> 15</li><li><strong>Int</strong> 2</li><li><strong>Wis</strong> 12</li><li><strong>Cha</strong> 6</li></ul><br /><ul class=\"sbcSemicolonList\" data-content=\"base-attack\"><li><strong>Base Atk</strong>+0</li><li><strong>CMB</strong> +0</li><li><strong>CMD</strong> 11  (15 vs. trip) </li></ul><br />  <strong>Feats</strong><ul class=\"sbcCommaList\" data-content=\"feats\">  <li>Skill Focus <ul class=\"sbcCommaList sbcParensWrappedList\">  <li>Perception</li>  </ul></li>  </ul><br />   <strong>Skills</strong><ul class=\"sbcCommaList\" data-content=\"skills\">  <li>Acrobatics +1 (+9 jumping)</li>  <li>Perception +8</li>  <li>Survival +1 (+5 scent tracking)</li>  </ul>  <br />     </div>  <div class=\"sbcSection\" data-content=\"ecology\"><h4>Ecology</h4><hr />  <strong>Environment</strong>   any <br />   <strong>Organization</strong>  solitary, pair, or pack (3-12)<br />   <strong>Treasure</strong>  none   <br />  </div>      <div class=\"sbcSection\" data-content=\"description\"><h4> Description </h4><hr /><div class=\"sbcPreWrap\">\nThe normal dog statistics presented here describe any small dog of about 20-50 pounds in weight. They can also be used for small wild canines such as coyotes, jackals, and feral dogs.\n\nIn the wild, dogs are vicious and territorial creatures. Yet even more harrowing than a pack of wild dogs is the rabid dog. Rabies often affects animals like bats, wolverines, and rats, but the transformation of a normally friendly family pet goes through when it becomes rabid makes the dog perhaps the most notorious of the disease's classic carriers.\n\nA rabid creature can transmit rabies to a victim with a bite. Its CR increases by 1 (or up one step, in the case of a creature whose CR is less than 1).\n\nRabies Type disease, injury; Save Fortitude DC 14 Onset 2d6 weeks; Frequency 1/day Effect 1 Con damage plus 1d3 Wis damage (minimum reduction to 1 Wis); Cure 2 consecutive saves\n</div></div>  </div><hr class=\"sbcBorder\" /></div><p></p></div><br /><hr /><div class=\"rawInputContainer\" style=\"margin-top:15px\"><h2 style=\"text-align:middle;border:none;text-transform:uppercase;color:#000\">RAW INPUT</h2><hr /><pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:14px\">    Dog (CR 0.33)\nSource PFRPG Bestiary \nCR 1/3 \nXP 135 \nN Small animal  \nInit +1; Senses low-light vision, scent; Perception +8   \nDefense   \nAC 13, touch 12, flat-footed 12 (+1 Dex, +1 natural, +1 size)\n\nhp 6 (1d8+2)\n\nFort +4, Ref +3, Will +1   \nOffense   \nSpd 40 ft. \nMelee bite +2 (1d4+1)\n\n\n\nStatistics   \nStr 13, Dex 13, Con 15, Int 2, Wis 12, Cha 6 \nBase Atk +0; CMB +0; CMD 11 (15 vs. trip)\n\nFeats Skill Focus (Perception)\n\nSkills Acrobatics +1 (+9 jumping), Perception +8, Survival +1 (+5 scent tracking); Racial Modifiers +4 Acrobatics when jumping, +4 Survival when tracking by scent   \nEcology   \nEnvironment  any \nOrganization solitary, pair, or pack (3-12)\n\nTreasure none   \nDescription\n\nThe normal dog statistics presented here describe any small dog of about 20-50 pounds in weight. They can also be used for small wild canines such as coyotes, jackals, and feral dogs.\n\nIn the wild, dogs are vicious and territorial creatures. Yet even more harrowing than a pack of wild dogs is the rabid dog. Rabies often affects animals like bats, wolverines, and rats, but the transformation of a normally friendly family pet goes through when it becomes rabid makes the dog perhaps the most notorious of the disease's classic carriers.\n\nA rabid creature can transmit rabies to a victim with a bite. Its CR increases by 1 (or up one step, in the case of a creature whose CR is less than 1).\n\nRabies Type disease, injury; Save Fortitude DC 14 Onset 2d6 weeks; Frequency 1/day Effect 1 Con damage plus 1d3 Wis damage (minimum reduction to 1 Wis); Cure 2 consecutive saves\n    </pre></div>"},"cr":{"base":0.33},"xp":{"value":0}},"skills":{"acr":{"ability":"dex","rt":false,"acp":true,"rank":0},"apr":{"ability":"int","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"art":{"ability":"int","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"blf":{"ability":"cha","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"clm":{"ability":"str","rt":false,"acp":true,"rank":0},"crf":{"ability":"int","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"dip":{"ability":"cha","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"dev":{"ability":"dex","rt":true,"acp":true,"rank":0},"dis":{"ability":"cha","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"esc":{"ability":"dex","rt":false,"acp":true,"rank":0},"fly":{"ability":"dex","rt":false,"acp":true,"rank":0},"han":{"ability":"cha","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"hea":{"ability":"wis","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"int":{"ability":"cha","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"kar":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"kdu":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"ken":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"kge":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"khi":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"klo":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"kna":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"kno":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"kpl":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"kre":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"lin":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"lor":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"per":{"ability":"wis","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":1},"prf":{"ability":"cha","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"pro":{"ability":"wis","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"rid":{"ab